\section{URL enumeration}{

KOTKAS is a server-rendered (jQuery / Bootstrap, not a SPA) Django-style
application. Index listings paginate via a numeric offset on the \verb{qs=}
query parameter (page size = 40, server-controlled); each page is one HTML
GET that lists titles, regions, initiation dates, statuses, and
developers/organisers. Detail pages live at
\verb{/kmh/kmh_view?kmh_id=<id>} (KMH) and \verb{/kmh/ksh_view?ksh_id=<id>} (KSH);
every field a downstream classifier needs (full title, narrative summary,
developer/proponent, decider/competent authority, KOV municipality,
geometry, attachment URLs) is on that page already.
}

\section{Geometry}{

Every detail record carries its activity area as an inline GeoJSON
geometry, embedded in a hidden form input (\verb{#activity_area_geojson}).
Coordinates are in \strong{EPSG:3301} (Estonian Coordinate System of 1997 /
L-EST97), the standard projected CRS for Estonia. When
\code{write_sidecar = TRUE}, the geometry is saved next to the sidecar as
\verb{<document_id>.geometry.geojson}. The sidecar carries \code{geometry_path}
(absolute path to the .geojson) and \code{geometry_crs} (\code{"EPSG:3301"}).

The GeoJSON is written with the GeoJSON-2008 \code{crs} member naming
\verb{urn:ogc:def:crs:EPSG::3301}; tools like QGIS / \code{sf::read_sf()} read this
fine, even though RFC 7946 deprecated the field. Coordinates are kept in
the source CRS — reproject downstream with \code{sf} if you need WGS84.
}

\section{Attachments}{

Each detail page exposes a \emph{Dokumendid} table whose rows have a direct,
public download URL of the form
\verb{https://kotkas.envir.ee/kmh/<kmh|ksh>_file_download?<kmh_id|ksh_id>=<id>&attachment_id=<aid>}
(no authentication needed). Documents are grouped by their portal \emph{Liik}
(type) column — common ones include \emph{Algatamise otsus} (initiation
decision), \emph{Programm} (assessment programme), \emph{Programmi otsus}
(programme decision), \emph{Aruanne} (report), \emph{Aruande otsus} (report
decision). The set is open-ended; the handler discovers whatever types a
record has and emits one \verb{attachment_urls_<slug>} / \verb{local_path_<slug>}
list-column per discovered type. The slug is the \emph{Liik} string with
Estonian diacritics transliterated, lowercased, and non-alphanumerics
collapsed to underscores. \code{attachment_urls} / \code{local_path} remain the
deduplicated union (required by the schema).
}

